  era: "c. 2600 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Mohenjo-daro
  text: On the Indus in Sindh, Pakistan, Mohenjo-daro was one of the largest cities, perhaps home to forty thousand people. Its Great Bath, grid streets and drains are famous, and it is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Its name means mound of the dead.
